      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm having some trouble with an iam policy for an s3 bucket. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to it but i keep getting an \"access denied\" error in the cloudwatch logs even though i added the s3:PutObject permission. here is the policy i'm using:\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\ncan u take a look and tell me what i'm missing? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your IAM policy for the S3 bucket only grants the \"s3:PutObject\" permission, which is necessary for Lambda to log to S3. However, when allowing Lambda to create log data, you also need to grant permissions to log to CloudWatch (s3:PutObject under “arn:aws:s3:us-east-1:*”:*/* is required for Lambda logs).\n\nYou must include a statement granting permissions for Lambda to put log events to CloudWatch logs in the same region as your bucket. Additionally, you need to ensure your bucket name, region, and resource ARNs match your actual setup. Here is the updated policy:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"s3:GetBucketLocation\",\n        \"s3:ListBucket\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket/*\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"logs:PutLogEvents\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:logs:us-east",
